Two separate issues:

**1. `StaticResource` won't update at runtime.**
`StaticResource` resolves once at XAML load time. Switch to `DynamicResource` so bindings re-evaluate when you swap the merged dictionary:

```xml
<!-- ✗ --> <Label TextColor="{StaticResource PrimaryText}" />
<!-- ✓ --> <Label TextColor="{DynamicResource PrimaryText}" />
```

Then swap themes by replacing the merged dictionary at runtime:

```csharp
var mergedDicts = Application.Current.Resources.MergedDictionaries;
mergedDicts.Clear();
mergedDicts.Add(useDark ? new DarkTheme() : new LightTheme());
```

**2. Activity restart on system theme change.**
Android destroys and recreates the activity when `uiMode` changes. Prevent this by adding to your `MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
[Activity(ConfigurationChanges = ConfigChanges.UiMode)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

This tells Android your app handles the change itself. Then detect the system switch with:

```csharp
public override void OnConfigurationChanged(Configuration newConfig)
{
    base.OnConfigurationChanged(newConfig);
    bool isDark = (newConfig.UiMode & UiMode.NightMask) == UiMode.NightYes;
    // swap your ResourceDictionary here
}
```

**TL;DR:** `StaticResource` → `DynamicResource` for anything theme-dependent, and handle `ConfigChanges.UiMode` to avoid the full restart.
